+### 5.9 conversation_list
+
+Answers a `list_conversations` request with a page of conversation metadata.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "conversation_list",
+  "conversations": [
+    {
+      "sessionId": "s2",
+      "createdAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
+      "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:02:00.000Z",
+      "entryCount": 4
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+| Field           | Type     | Description                           |
+| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | string   | `"conversation_list"`                 |
+| `conversations` | object[] | Summaries of the user's conversations |
+
+Each summary carries:
+
+| Field        | Type   | Description                                                |
+| ------------ | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `sessionId`  | string | The conversation's id, for reconnecting with `?sessionId=` |
+| `createdAt`  | string | ISO 8601 creation time                                     |
+| `updatedAt`  | string | ISO 8601 last activity time                                |
+| `entryCount` | number | Total entries in the conversation                          |
+
+Authorization:
+The list ALWAYS carries the authenticated user's own conversations. Any `userId` field in the request frame is ignored ([validated by: answers list_conversations for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+
+Failures:
+
+- With `transport.history` disabled, or against a store that cannot list conversations, the server answers `error` with code `UNSUPPORTED` ([validated by: answers an empty conversation_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L93), [validated by: answers with UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L149)).
+- A store failure is reported as `SERVER_ERROR` ([validated by: answers an empty conversation_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L93)).
